  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1121 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nSouthwesterly flow looks to continue for Friday as most models\ncontinue see a new upper-level trough push across the Western\nUntied States. This flow should keep a majority of Friday dry and\nwarm for the Panhandles with afternoon highs in the 60s. By late\nFriday however, present models do see this flow come to an end\nwith the arrival of this trough and its associated cold front. At\nthis time ensembles are not to thrilled on the idea any\nprecipitation with chances this weekend below 10 percent. However,\nsome of the recent deterministic runs have tried push some\nprecipitation into the Panhandles, especially in our northwest and\nsoutheast. Regardless, better chances may follow next Monday and\nTuesday as models continue to trend towards yet another system\nmoving across the area. Otherwise, look for cooler temperatures to\nfollow behind the expected front with highs in the 50s for the\nweekend and 40s and 50s for next week.",
